  "description": "Kopia explicitly uses DYNAMIC-4M-BUZHASH, disabled content compression and AES256-GCM-HMAC-SHA256 encryption. Gutch uses a nominal 4 MiB FastCDC target, no compression, 16 MiB bundles and no encryption. Bounds, metadata, hashes and packing differ. Kopia recovery requests native extra-file deletion. Fresh repositories and isolated caches. Four workers where exposed; native Borg/BPT scheduling. One warm-up and 1 rotating measured repetitions; profiling off. Measurement contract 2 separates content repair, preserved-mtime damage, extra-file cleanup and full restoration. Strict source-derived SHA-256 validation follows every supported operation; both native and validation-inclusive durations are reported. Unsupported operations receive no timing.",
